Subject: Drop the unused point cursor in ft_stroke_border_get_counts()

ft_stroke_border_get_counts() advances a `point` cursor it never reads.
GCC's -Wall reports it (-Wunused-but-set-variable), which R CMD check
counts as a significant warning. FreeType's own ftstroke.c dropped the
variable for the same reason.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §14. Offered upstream.

--- a/plutovg/source/plutovg-ft-stroker.c
+++ b/plutovg/source/plutovg-ft-stroker.c
@@ -532,11 +532,10 @@
     PVG_FT_UInt  num_contours = 0;
 
     PVG_FT_UInt    count = border->num_points;
-    PVG_FT_Vector* point = border->points;
     PVG_FT_Byte*   tags = border->tags;
     PVG_FT_Int     in_contour = 0;
 
-    for (; count > 0; count--, num_points++, point++, tags++) {
+    for (; count > 0; count--, num_points++, tags++) {
         if (tags[0] & PVG_FT_STROKE_TAG_BEGIN) {
             if (in_contour != 0) goto Fail;
 
